   "tag": "Stop 1",
   "h2": "What counts as bullying?",
   "body_html": "<p class=\"big\"><span class=\"hl p\">Bullying</span> is:</p><ul><li><b>Repeated</b> — not a one-off.</li><li><b>Hurtful</b> — meant to harm.</li><li><b>Power imbalance</b> — bully has more strength, status or numbers.</li></ul>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Stop 2",
   "h2": "Four types",
   "body_html": "<ul><li><span class=\"hl p\">Physical</span> — hits, pushing, taking things.</li><li><span class=\"hl p\">Verbal</span> — insults, threats.</li><li><span class=\"hl y\">Social</span> — leaving someone out, rumours.</li><li><span class=\"hl y\">Cyberbullying</span> — nasty messages, screenshots, fake accounts.</li></ul>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Stop 3",
   "h2": "Signs to spot",
   "body_html": "<p>Warning signs in a friend:</p><ul><li>Not wanting to go to school.</li><li>Losing things, bruises.</li><li>Mood changes.</li><li>Hiding their phone.</li></ul><p>If you see it, you're a <b>bystander</b> — and you can help. 🛑</p>"
  }
